  "notes": "**The browser asks once about new site access.** This version lets the extension read the video and social sites listed below from install. After the update, Chrome turns the extension off until you approve it: open the extensions menu, choose DoRaptim, and accept the new permissions. Firefox asks in the same way. Nothing is read on other sites unless you choose **All sites** in Settings. **Browser toolbar**: closing a tab while DoRaptim updates its video count no longer produces an unhandled background error. **Download compatibility**: the engine can negotiate HTTP/2 with CDNs that refuse its HTTP/1.1 requests for HLS playlists or segments. Each part of a download, and each stream piece fetched at once, still gets a connection of its own over HTTP/2, so multi-connection downloads stay as fast as before.",
